 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049346 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429160 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049346 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429161 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049346 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429162 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049346 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429163 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049346 #edb/ref 1031 "Properties of Line Integrals of Vector-Valued Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049346 #edb/ref 1033 3704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049346 #edb/ref 1034 0.7481948998356526 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049346 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "ed9d339c-fde4-545b-86b4-381d2f85203f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050687 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050687 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050687 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050687 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050687 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429196 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050687 #edb/ref 1031 "Properties of Line Integrals With Respect to X and Y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050687 #edb/ref 1033 3708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050687 #edb/ref 1034 0.7115353819465683 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050687 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5f0fbf1a-01fe-5c95-8b44-55eb40e24c08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428614 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428615 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428616 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428617 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428618 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1031 "Line Integrals With Respect to X and Y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1033 2109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051000 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "789238e2-4251-5080-bbc3-e713bd84a64b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179593 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9525" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179593 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x,$ where $C=C_1 \\cup C_2$ is the path comprising of two line segments, as shown below.\n\n![](images/3d/3d408de0d50e2688aa0b35d8af39b6847cfdf21d5ec583320f0204384304fbc8.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179593 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "30d54dcc-49a2-5cd0-9eb9-659413ed5c67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179593 #edb/ref 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_2$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $x_1$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $x_2 = -3$ and $x_1 = 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1 = (-3) - 3 = -6.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179594 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9526" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179594 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y,$ where $C$ is the path along the semicircle of radius $3,$ traversed from the point $(3,0)$ to the point $(-3,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/ca/ca97546ecaf9e37bee53fcc2b0c66962cff67a91ee9b117cc8ac8531efa23efc.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179594 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d799bcde-dbf0-580e-921b-18e56d729ea1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179594 #edb/ref 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1,\n$$\n\nwhere $y_2$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $y_1$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $y_2 = 0$ and $y_1 = 0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1 =  0 - 0 = 0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179595 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9527" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179595 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= 8$ and $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= -2,$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x$ given that $C = C_1\\cup C_2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179595 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e1d24f1c-4b7c-5c5e-bf93-7f9e76dffdf2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179595 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C = C_1\\cup C_2$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = -\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = \\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x + \\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =-(-2)-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =2-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x = -6.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179731 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051000 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179731 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186179999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179731 #edb/ref 